Constant approximable maps valued at a fixed ideal element.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`constMap`).** The constant approximable map at an ideal element relates a domain neighbourhood to a codomain neighbourhood precisely when the latter belongs to that element.

*Proof.* Domain and codomain membership, master, intersection on the right, and monotonicity follow from the filter axioms of the value. ∎

**Theorem (`constMap_rel`).** Membership in the constant-map relation is domain neighbourhood membership together with membership of the value in the codomain neighbourhood.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎

**Theorem (`toElementMap_constMap`).** The elementwise action of a constant map is the constant function with that value.

*Proof.* Compare membership: the forward direction unpacks a witnessing domain neighbourhood; the converse evaluates at the domain master. ∎
